 a town on the Po in Piedmont, north-western Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/casamance"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/casamance.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Casamance</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Casamance is the region of southern Senegal lying between The Gambia and Guinea-Bissau, drained by the Casamance River.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/casbah-of-algiers"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/casbah-of-algiers.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Casbah of Algiers</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">The Casbah of Algiers is the old walled town of Algiers, rising on a steep hill above the harbour and crowned by the citadel built in the Ottoman period.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/casilinum"><span class="enc-name">Casilinum</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Casilinum was an ancient town in Campania, southern Italy, at a crossing of the Volturno river on the Via Appia.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/casimir-i-of-kuyavia"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/casimir-i-of-kuyavia.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Casimir I of Kuyavia</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Casimir I of Kuyavia was a Piast duke, son of Konrad I of Masovia, who received Kuyavia in 1233 and Łęczyca after his father's death in 1247.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/casimir-i-of-opole"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/casimir-i-of-opole.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Casimir I of Opole</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Casimir I of Opole (c. 1178–1230) was a Piast duke of Opole and Racibórz in Upper Silesia from 1211, a son of Mieszko IV Tanglefoot.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/casimir-ii-of-leczyca"><span class="enc-name">Casimir II of Łęczyca</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Casimir II of Łęczyca (c. 1261–1294) was a Polish prince of the Piast dynasty, a son of Casimir I of Kuyavia.</span></a></li></ul>
